WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:13.500
[Music]

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:17.460
[Narrator:] We are convinced that fulltime
health service can be rendered New York State

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:22.189
citizens most effectively under a district
plan of administration.

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:27.080
Thirty state health districts and subdistricts are now in operation 

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:29.520
or will be in operation at an early date.

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:34.649
The five county health departments are integral parts of their respective districts.

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:42.100
Suitable quarters are provided for district offices, such as those at Albany and Buffalo.

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:47.060
A fulltime district state health officer
is in charge of each district.

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:51.600
Civil service qualifications for new district officers include a medical degree, 

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:56.380
a postgraduate course in public health, and five years fulltime experience.

00:00:57.320 --> 00:01:02.160
The district officer is the commissioner's
representative and authorized to act for him.

00:01:02.170 --> 00:01:05.670
He has available for technical advice the
directors of the eleven divisions

00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:08.020
and two district health directors.

00:01:08.030 --> 00:01:12.520
Besides the district officer, the average
district staff includes an assistant district officer,

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:15.860
a district supervising nurse, one
or more engineers, 

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:19.440
supervising-in-field public health nurses, and a clerical staff.

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:25.020
Full records are kept in all district offices,
such as syphilis and tuberculosis registers,

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:28.049
maintained and checked according to the status of each case.

00:01:28.049 --> 00:01:31.460
District offices conduct the state program
through 798 local

00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:34.600
health officers and five county health commissioners.

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:37.500
There are frequent conferences with local health officers.

00:01:37.509 --> 00:01:42.289
When serious epidemics or unusual circumstances
occur, assistance is given to the district

00:01:42.289 --> 00:01:46.169
officer by temporary assignments from other
districts, or the central office.

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:50.619
District staffs are flexible and not subject to local authority.

00:01:50.619 --> 00:01:54.320
An important function of the district officer
is the preliminary field training of

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:58.570
young physicians, and participation and selection of physicians for academic postgraduate

00:01:58.570 --> 00:02:00.500
training and careers in public health.

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:05.220
The district state supervising nurse supervises
nurses employed by the department, as well

00:02:05.229 --> 00:02:10.070
as many employed locally. She has a responsibility
for the training and selection of nurses,

00:02:10.070 --> 00:02:12.870
similar to that of the district officer for physicians.

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:17.769
The district officer has a part in all the
departments' major activity.

00:02:17.769 --> 00:02:23.389
[ Music ]

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:28.380
New York State is now conducting an experimental
field study to determine the feasibility of

00:02:28.390 --> 00:02:34.520
nursing delivery service as part of the generalized
nursing program in a rural county.

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:39.000
Because of persistently high infant mortality, preponderance of home delivery,

00:02:39.020 --> 00:02:43.640
and maternal deaths chiefly in rural sections, St. Lawrence County was selected.

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:48.200
Conferences were held of state and local health officials and with local physicians,

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:51.790
hospital, and welfare representatives. The country was zoned for accessibility. 

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:54.960
Ten nurses and a supervising nurse who was midwife-trained were assigned.

00:02:55.490 --> 00:03:00.530
The nurses were equipped with cars, fitted bags, and electric lanterns as well as strong snow shovels.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:05.620
Nurses instruct prospective mothers and help them make their preparations.

00:03:05.820 --> 00:03:11.280
[ Music ]

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:15.900
Obstetric packages for use by the doctors
in home deliveries were made and assembled

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:19.420
in WPA sewing rooms, and by volunteer groups of women. 

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:24.260
The nurses supervised the work and assembled the packages for sterilizing at the local milk plant.

00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:28.820
[ Music ]

00:03:28.820 --> 00:03:34.170
The doctor, arriving for a delivery, finds
a nurse in charge, room and patient prepared,

00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:38.710
and hot water ready. Towels and sterile supplies are waiting in the package. 

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:44.720
The electric lantern is better than the kerosene lamp, and the nurse is a willing, efficient helper.

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:50.700
Nurse returns next morning to bathe baby, care for mother, and instruct neighbor or relative.

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:54.560
This doctor believes the service
is meeting a real need 

00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:56.600
and appreciates the work of the nurses,

00:03:56.610 --> 00:04:02.490
who in addition to general duties, have assisted at 84 home deliveries and supervised

00:04:02.490 --> 00:04:07.050
431 patients during the first six months of the demonstration.

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:18.760
[ Music ]

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:24.620
Engineering is a major branch of public health
work. Reduction in typhoid fever in New York State

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:29.250
has been due in large measure to the control exercised by the Division of Sanitation

00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:31.770
over water, milk, and sewage disposal.

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:36.520
Engineers supervise the sanitary quality of water supplied to more than twelve million persons.

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:40.699
Over 90 percent of the water consumed in New York State receives treatment. 

00:04:40.699 --> 00:04:44.159
Many water purification plants have been constructed as a result of recommendations 

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:46.040
made by department engineers.

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:50.400
Water supplies are inspected frequently and
subjected to routine bacteriological tests

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:51.700
at regular intervals.

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:57.180
In milk-borne disease outbreaks, all suspected
cows are examined by a department veterinarian.

00:04:57.520 --> 00:05:01.480
For assured safety, the department urges the use of pasteurized milk. 

00:05:01.560 --> 00:05:04.240
Pasteurizing plants are inspected frequently.

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:09.700
Routine tests used in laboratory-controlled
milk supplies are the direct microscopic count

00:05:09.710 --> 00:05:14.449
to determine quality of the raw product, the
phosphatase test to determine the thoroughness

00:05:14.449 --> 00:05:20.139
of pasteurization of the milk, and the
Coli test to detect contamination after pasteurization.

00:05:20.139 --> 00:05:24.990
Pollution of streams is being abated by requiring installation [?] sewage treatment plant, regularly

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:29.460
inspected by department engineers. More than one hundred plants have been constructed

00:05:29.460 --> 00:05:32.569
in New York State since 1930.

00:05:32.569 --> 00:05:37.349
Plans for all sewerage improvements must receive approval of the Division of Sanitation prior to construction.

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:41.840
In five years, the value of works represented by such plans has amounted

00:05:41.849 --> 00:05:43.870
to more than one hundred million dollars.

00:05:43.870 --> 00:05:47.360
Two thousand swimming pools throughout the
state are supervised by the division as well

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:50.160
as 3,000 summer and tourist camps,
which provide accommodations

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:52.840
annually for two million persons.

00:05:52.840 --> 00:05:57.330
Routine work of the Division of Sanitation
is expedited by the assignment of district

00:05:57.330 --> 00:06:01.960
engineers and milk sanitarians to the staff of the various state health districts,

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:05.760
enabling prompt service to be rendered in
connection with any sanitary problems

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:09.100
arising within the district.

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:17.400
[ Music ]

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:24.080
New York State's program for the control of
pneumonia embraces a variety of activities.

00:06:24.090 --> 00:06:27.979
Anti-pneumococcus serums for the treatment of the five types for which it has been proved

00:06:27.979 --> 00:06:32.259
of value are produced and dispensed at no cost to physicians.

00:06:32.259 --> 00:06:37.999
Diagnostic serums for six types are dispensed to 112 approved laboratories and typing stations.

00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:41.840
Sputum is examined immediately by the Neufeld technique.

00:06:41.849 --> 00:06:45.169
Virulent flecks are mixed with each type of serum and examined. 

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:48.380
Blood cultures are highly important in cases of pneumonia.

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:52.020
Extensive graduate medical education is being undertaken, 

00:06:52.160 --> 00:06:55.219
in cooperation with the New York State Medical Society.

00:06:55.219 --> 00:06:59.799
Every available means of reaching the medical profession is being utilized

00:06:59.860 --> 00:07:03.160
in the belief that earlier diagnosis and wider and more adequate use of

00:07:03.180 --> 00:07:06.149
the serums now available may result.

00:07:07.809 --> 00:07:12.159
The need for teaching the general public the seriousness of certain of the early symptoms

00:07:12.159 --> 00:07:15.819
of pneumonia and the urgency of medical care is recognized. 

00:07:16.140 --> 00:07:22.539
The mere availability of serum is insufficient, unless an enlightened public makes its early use possible.

00:07:22.539 --> 00:07:27.740
Skillful nursing care is important. Public
health nurses throughout the state are devoting

00:07:27.740 --> 00:07:33.069
increasing time to bedside care, as well as
to teaching demonstrations for pneumonia cases.

00:07:33.500 --> 00:07:37.520
The New York State Nurses Association is cooperating
with the state health department

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:40.380
in graduate education of its members.

00:07:40.389 --> 00:07:43.879
Research has resulted in further advances
in the methods of production and refinement

00:07:43.879 --> 00:07:45.309
of the therapeutic serums.

00:07:45.309 --> 00:07:50.740
A series of sixteen hundred and sixty Type1 pneumonia cases, treated with serum produced

00:07:50.740 --> 00:07:55.740
and dispensed by the department, was accumulated during the first twenty months of the program.

00:07:55.740 --> 00:08:00.219
Fairly complete data are available on all
of these, and their careful analysis gives

00:08:00.219 --> 00:08:05.499
promise of adding substantially to our knowledge of the limitations, requisites, and potentialities

00:08:05.499 --> 00:08:08.179
of serum treatment as a method of pneumonia control.

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:16.300
[ Music ]

00:08:16.639 --> 00:08:21.569
The state of New York owns and maintains the
oldest cancer research laboratory in the world,

00:08:21.569 --> 00:08:23.469
established in 1898.

00:08:23.909 --> 00:08:30.180
This hospital located in Buffalo, and called
The State Institute for the Study of Malignant Disease,

00:08:30.180 --> 00:08:34.060
has research facilities in all branches
of science and a bed capacity of a hundred

00:08:34.060 --> 00:08:36.650
and thirty after completion of a new wing.

00:08:36.650 --> 00:08:41.550
The state institute is equipped with a complete
surgical department and modern X-ray and

00:08:41.550 --> 00:08:46.410
radium appliances for the diagnosis and treatment of malignant disease.

00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:51.940
[ Music ]

00:08:51.940 --> 00:08:56.360
There are eight grams of radium at the state institute--two in solution, 

00:08:56.400 --> 00:08:58.460
and six grams of the insoluble salt. 

00:08:58.620 --> 00:09:01.840
As much radium as is possessed by any hospital in the world.

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:07.020
As radium in solution disintegrate, it gives
off a gas which can be utilized only after

00:09:07.030 --> 00:09:12.210
it is removed from the solution by means of oil and mercury pumps.

00:09:13.080 --> 00:09:18.520
Modern shockproof x-ray machines are available for the treatment of malignant growth.

00:09:23.460 --> 00:09:30.300
Last year 3,645 new patients were admitted to this hospital for diagnosis and treatment. 

00:09:30.400 --> 00:09:33.040
This service is free to all residents of New York State

00:09:33.040 --> 00:09:37.410
who are recommended for examination and treatment by their family physicians.

00:09:37.410 --> 00:09:41.620
An extensive educational program is being carried on for the purpose of dispelling

00:09:41.620 --> 00:09:45.320
fear of cancer, and impressing upon the laity that there is a cure 

00:09:45.340 --> 00:09:48.240
if the disease is recognized in its early stages.

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:54.720
It is always borne in mind that this is primarily an institute for the study of malignant disease

00:09:54.730 --> 00:09:58.890
and every opportunity is embraced to conduct a continuous program of research 

00:09:58.890 --> 00:10:02.570
in the unsolved problems of cancer control.

00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:12.560
[ Music ]

00:10:12.560 --> 00:10:17.940
Since 1916, New York State has been rebuilding its crippled children and now spends more

00:10:17.950 --> 00:10:22.880
than one and a half million dollars annually
on their rehabilitation and education.

00:10:22.880 --> 00:10:26.820
Through efforts of the orthopedic nurses and
family physicians, they are brought to clinics

00:10:26.820 --> 00:10:30.420
for examination by an orthopedic surgeon.

00:10:30.420 --> 00:10:35.090
If a child has a condition that can definitely
be improved, arrangements are made to admit

00:10:35.090 --> 00:10:40.000
the youngster to a local institution that
meets the state requirements, or to the

00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:42.940
New York State Reconstruction Home at West Haverstraw.

00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:47.730
[ Music ]

00:10:47.800 --> 00:10:51.400
Here, specialized surgery is available when needed. 

00:10:54.440 --> 00:10:59.120
Hospital care by specially-trained nurses guards the child if an operation is necessary. 

00:10:59.800 --> 00:11:03.440
 Physiotherapy aids his recovery.

00:11:06.430 --> 00:11:10.310
Trained teachers work with him so that when he goes home he will be able to follow along

00:11:10.310 --> 00:11:16.120
with his schoolmates. Outside activities
keep the youngsters busy and happy.

00:11:16.120 --> 00:11:19.320
Some of them have reached a point where their
physical condition will permit them to

00:11:19.320 --> 00:11:22.160
carry on restricted activities on the playground.

00:11:22.820 --> 00:11:27.380
A twelve-piece orchestra furnishes music at
the institution and plays at the

00:11:27.460 --> 00:11:29.840
annual state health conference at Saratoga Springs.

00:11:29.840 --> 00:11:35.040
You are listening to it now, playing a selection which is used as the theme music of the

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:38.740
state health department's weekly radio program.

00:11:38.820 --> 00:11:44.680
[ Music ]

00:11:44.830 --> 00:11:49.590
When the patient is ready to leave the reconstruction
home, she is returned to her home and

00:11:49.590 --> 00:11:54.080
family physician under the care of the orthopedic nurse and a field clinic service

00:11:54.080 --> 00:11:57.400
conducted by the State Department of Health.

00:11:57.700 --> 00:12:07.320
[ Music ]

00:12:07.750 --> 00:12:12.610
New York state's tuberculosis case- finding program is based on the fact that the control

00:12:12.610 --> 00:12:16.550
of tuberculosis depends on the prevention
of spread of tuberculus infection.

00:12:17.200 --> 00:12:23.340
This can be accomplished by segregation, treatment,
and education of the open cases of tuberculosis

00:12:23.340 --> 00:12:26.440
and by going out into the field and finding
cases.

00:12:26.860 --> 00:12:32.020
Tuberculosis is a family problem and the most
fertile source for finding new cases

00:12:32.020 --> 00:12:36.920
is among close household contacts of those having the disease.

00:12:40.430 --> 00:12:45.550
Early discovery of tuberculosis means early recovery. To that end our efforts should be devoted.

00:12:46.180 --> 00:12:52.180
Early tuberculosis is not characterized
by any special signs or symptoms.

00:12:52.230 --> 00:12:56.550
And we should investigate other possible fertile
sources for finding early cases.

00:12:56.940 --> 00:12:58.540
These men have been x-rayed. 

00:12:59.400 --> 00:13:03.940
X-ray is our most valuable ally in discovering the disease in its earliest stages.

00:13:07.110 --> 00:13:12.270
And these workers, too, have been x-rayed.

00:13:12.270 --> 00:13:16.420
These normal school students, mostly young
women at the age of greatest perceptibility

00:13:16.420 --> 00:13:22.590
to adult-type pulmonary tuberculosis are tuberculin tested and x-rayed yearly until graduation.

00:13:22.590 --> 00:13:26.550
Consecutive admissions to general hospitals
are x-rayed.

00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:33.500
[ Music ]

00:13:33.500 --> 00:13:39.840
This patient had advanced disease when discovered. His treatment is prolonged, his prognosis is dubious.

00:13:39.840 --> 00:13:43.480
The cost to himself, family, and
community is great.

00:13:43.480 --> 00:13:47.700
On the other hand, this patient was discovered
early and after a suitable length of observation

00:13:47.700 --> 00:13:50.540
and treatment is well on the road to complete
rehabilitation. 

00:13:50.840 --> 00:13:55.660
It is real economy to spend money and effort to find the early case.

00:13:56.660 --> 00:14:06.180
[ Music ]

00:14:06.500 --> 00:14:11.420
Public health programs are effective only
so far as they are taken to, understood,

00:14:11.430 --> 00:14:13.570
and accepted by the public.

00:14:13.570 --> 00:14:17.490
Frequent press stories are released to news
services, local correspondents, and the 

00:14:17.490 --> 00:14:22.620
130 dailies and 540 weeklies in New York State.

00:14:22.620 --> 00:14:28.380
Health news is sent every week to fourteen
thousand physicians, nurses, hospitals, libraries,

00:14:28.380 --> 00:14:32.060
public health workers, and other interested individuals and agencies. 

00:14:32.100 --> 00:14:36.900
Qualified experts prepare special stories and pamphlets on health subjects.

00:14:36.910 --> 00:14:41.450
During the first nine months of 1937, one
million two hundred and seventy five thousand

00:14:41.450 --> 00:14:44.170
of these educational pamphlets were distributed.

00:14:44.480 --> 00:14:49.540
From the beginning, visual instruction has been foremost among health education aids in New York.

00:14:49.540 --> 00:14:53.900
Now, 16 and 35-millimeter cameras
record the progress of public health,

00:14:53.900 --> 00:14:59.260
and silent and sound projectors spread the story as told in a library of 50 film subjects.

00:14:59.260 --> 00:15:03.670
The health-mobile rolls over paved roads and country lanes with this equipment,

00:15:03.670 --> 00:15:08.150
as well as exhibits and displays and other portable educational material.

00:15:08.180 --> 00:15:13.160
Probably the most intimate approach into the homes of the people with the state's health message is radio.

00:15:13.200 --> 00:15:17.880
Each week since August 1933, health plays written, acted, and produced entirely

00:15:17.890 --> 00:15:23.630
within the State Department of Health have been presented from WGY Schenectady.

00:15:23.630 --> 00:15:28.670
Now, by means of electrical transcription
recordings, these programs are broadcast 

00:15:28.670 --> 00:15:32.610
throughout the state over a chain of 19 other radio stations.

00:15:34.560 --> 00:15:40.000
Then these electrical transcriptions are available
by means of portable sound equipment for use

00:15:40.010 --> 00:15:44.370
before granges, parent-teacher associations,
school classes, women's organizations,

00:15:44.480 --> 00:15:46.760
service clubs, and similar groups.

00:15:46.770 --> 00:15:51.220
From radio alone, since the beginning of the
weekly play series, responses have been received

00:15:51.220 --> 00:15:54.700
from 745 different cities and villages in the state. 

00:15:54.980 --> 00:15:58.540
Health education is reaching the people of New York State.

00:15:58.760 --> 00:16:22.400
[ Music ]

